Case Study 3: Campus Event Financial Planning
1. Problem Statement
Calculate total campus event execution expenses across venue, catering, equipment, transport, and certificates; incorporate participant contributions and sponsorship funding; and determine sponsorship shortfalls alongside break-even registration numbers.
2. Objectives
•	Aggregate fixed and variable expense components.
•	Compute net sponsorship gap or surplus.
•	Determine break-even participant count required at given registration fee.

3. Assumptions
•	Fixed costs include venue and equipment.
•	Variable costs per participant include catering and certificates.
4. Algorithm
1. Define venue cost, equipment cost, transport cost.
2. Define per-participant catering fee and certificate cost.
3. Calculate Total Fixed Cost = venue + equipment + transport.
4. Calculate Variable Cost per Person = catering + certificate.
5. Total Expenses = Fixed Cost + (Variable Cost * Expected Participants).
6. Net Revenue Required = Total Expenses - Sponsorship.
7. Break-Even Count = Fixed Cost / (Registration Fee - Variable Cost per Person).
